---
layout: page
---
{% assign snapshot = site.data.football_rivalries %}
{% assign record = snapshot.rivalries[page.rivalry] %}
{% assign first_team = record.teams[0] %}
{% assign second_team = record.teams[1] %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/team-rankings.css' | relative_url }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/football-tools.css' | relative_url }}">
<p class="rivalry-intro">
  {{ first_team }} and {{ second_team }} have {{ record.played }} recorded league meetings in this database, from
  <time datetime="{{ record.first.date }}">{{ record.first.date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</time> to
  <time datetime="{{ record.latest.date }}">{{ record.latest.date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</time>.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Scope:</strong> recorded English league matches only. Domestic cups, European competitions, friendlies and separate end-of-season test
  matches are not included. Club names follow the database's historical naming conventions.
</p>
<p class="rivalry-data-date">
  Generated from the results CSV on <time datetime="{{ snapshot.as_of }}">{{ snapshot.as_of | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</time>. The database contains
  results through <time datetime="{{ snapshot.database_through }}">{{ snapshot.database_through | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</time>. These records refresh
  with the site's automatic updates; they are not live scores.
</p>

<h2>Overall league head-to-head record</h2>
<p>
  Across {{ record.played }} recorded league meetings, {{ first_team }} have {{ record.wins[0] }} wins, {{ second_team }} have
  {{ record.wins[1] }} wins, and {{ record.draws }} matches have been drawn.
</p>
<table class="rivalry-table">
  <caption>
    All league meetings in this snapshot, at either club's home ground
  </caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Measure</th>
      <th scope="col">{{ first_team }}</th>
      <th scope="col">{{ second_team }}</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Wins</th>
      <td>{{ record.wins[0] }}</td>
      <td>{{ record.wins[1] }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Goals scored</th>
      <td>{{ record.goals[0] }}</td>
      <td>{{ record.goals[1] }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>
  The first recorded league meeting in this dataset was {{ record.first.home }}
  {{ record.first.home_goals }}–{{ record.first.away_goals }}
  {{ record.first.away }} on {{ record.first.date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }} ({{ record.first.division }}). The latest included meeting was
  {{ record.latest.home }}
  {{ record.latest.home_goals }}–{{ record.latest.away_goals }}
  {{ record.latest.away }} on {{ record.latest.date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}.
</p>

<section class="team-rankings football-tool rivalry-wins-chart" id="rivalry-wins" aria-labelledby="rivalry-wins-title">
  <div class="football-panel">
    <h2 id="rivalry-wins-title">Wins over time</h2>
    <p class="rankings-note">
      Cumulative league wins. Hover or tap to see a match; click a team's name to hide or show its line. Swipe vertically to scroll the page.
    </p>
    <p class="rankings-note" id="rivalry-chart-status" role="status">
      The chart requires JavaScript and its chart libraries. All statistics and recent results remain available below.
    </p>
    <div class="football-history-chart" id="rivalry-chart-display" hidden>
      <canvas
        id="rivalry-history"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Cumulative wins across {{ record.played }} league meetings. {{ first_team | escape }}: {{ record.wins[0] }} wins; {{ second_team | escape }}: {{ record.wins[1] }} wins."
      ></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script type="application/json" id="rivalry-chart-data">
  {"teams": {{ record.teams | jsonify | replace: '<', '\u003c' }}, "rows": {{ record.win_history | jsonify | replace: '<', '\u003c' }}}
</script>

<h2>Home and away records</h2>
<div class="rivalry-table-scroll">
  <table class="rivalry-table">
    <caption>
      Venue split: the win columns always refer to the named club, not the home or away side
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Home team</th>
        <th scope="col">Played</th>
        <th scope="col">{{ first_team }} wins</th>
        <th scope="col">Draws</th>
        <th scope="col">{{ second_team }} wins</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for venue in record.venue %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{{ venue.home }}</th>
          <td>{{ venue.played }}</td>
          <td>{{ venue.wins[0] }}</td>
          <td>{{ venue.draws }}</td>
          <td>{{ venue.wins[1] }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p>
  A home/away split is descriptive, not a forecast. Read about
  <a href="{% post_url 2025-01-13-Home_advantage_in_English_football %}">how home advantage has changed in English football</a> before treating a
  long-run record as a measure of today's teams.
</p>

<h2>Premier League era</h2>
<p>
  Restricting the record to top-tier league meetings from August 1992 gives {{ record.premier.played }} matches: {{ record.premier.wins[0] }}
  {{ first_team }} wins, {{ record.premier.draws }} draws and {{ record.premier.wins[1] }}
  {{ second_team }} wins. This is a subset of the all-history total, not an additional set of matches.
</p>

<h2>Biggest league wins</h2>
{% for biggest in record.biggest %}
  {% assign club = record.teams[forloop.index0] %}
  {% if biggest.matches.size > 0 %}
    <h3>{{ club }}: {{ biggest.margin }}-goal margin</h3>
    <ul>
      {% for match in biggest.matches %}
        <li>
          {{ match.home }}
          {{ match.home_goals }}–{{ match.away_goals }}
          {{ match.away }}, {{ match.date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }} ({{ match.division }}).
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  {% else %}
    <h3>{{ club }}</h3>
    <p>No league wins recorded against {{ record.teams[forloop.rindex0] }} in this dataset.</p>
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
<p>“Biggest” means the largest winning margin; every tied record in the dataset is listed.</p>

<h2>Recent league results</h2>
<table class="rivalry-table">
  <caption>
    The
    {{ record.recent.size }}
    latest recorded league meetings, newest first; home team shown first
  </caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Date</th>
      <th scope="col">Home</th>
      <th scope="col">Score</th>
      <th scope="col">Away</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for match in record.recent %}
      <tr>
        <td>
          <time datetime="{{ match.date }}">{{ match.date | date: '%-d %b %Y' }}</time>
        </td>
        <td>{{ match.home }}</td>
        <td>{{ match.home_goals }}–{{ match.away_goals }}</td>
        <td>{{ match.away }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Explore the full match history</h2>
<p>
  <a href="{{ '/h2h' | relative_url }}?team1={{ first_team | url_encode }}&amp;team2={{ second_team | url_encode }}"
    >Compare {{ first_team }} and {{ second_team }} in the interactive head-to-head tool</a
  >
  to see the current database, all recorded meetings, season/date filters and charts. You can also
  <a href="{{ '/leaguetable' | relative_url }}">reconstruct the league table for a season</a> or
  <a href="{{ '/teamRankings' | relative_url }}">compare team-strength ratings over time</a>.
</p>

<script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.8/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/luxon@3.5.0/build/global/luxon.min.js"></script>
<script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chartjs-adapter-luxon@1.3.1/dist/chartjs-adapter-luxon.umd.min.js"></script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/team-rankings-data.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/football-tools.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/football-win-history.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/rivalry-chart.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
